WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.900
After the soul-rending gut-punch of Infinity
War, Ant-Man and the Wasp is like an afternoon

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.480
trip to Baskin-Robbins.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.099
It's colorful, splashy, and fun, without too
much emotional weight.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.720
"Hiya champ, how was school today?"

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.000
(laughs)

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.900
Still, that definitely isn't to say that everything
got a neat resolution at the end of the movie.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.640
True to form for Marvel films, Ant-Man and
the Wasp ends on a slippery slope covered

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.820
in cliffhangers and unanswered questions.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.749
Well, grab some orange slices and watch out
for tardigrades, because we're diving deep

00:00:27.749 --> 00:00:31.589
into the Quantum Realm to clear up some of
the nagging questions you might have had after

00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:35.730
seeing Ant-Man and the Wasp - obviously, spoilers
ahead.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:36.730
Wasp evolution

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.610
Clearly, the Quantum Realm is a crazy place.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:43.800
We first saw how bonkers it is in the first
Ant-Man, when Scott Lang nearly got lost after

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.360
shrinking between the molecules of Yellowjacket's
suit.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.640
It gets even worse when Hank Pym takes his
Innerspace bus into the Quantum Realm in Ant-Man

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:51.640
and the Wasp.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:52.640
Here's a rough reenactment:

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.170
"Here we go!"

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:58.510
Once Hank's in there, he almost immediately
starts losing his mind.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.240
Thankfully, Janet shows up just in time to
fix him with her new quantum powers.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.760
So… what was up with that?

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.790
As Janet briefly explained, the three decades
she spent in the Realm forced her to evolve

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.180
in some strange ways to deal with the madness
of the Quantum Realm.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:15.510
Part of that evolution apparently gave her
the ability to influence quantum particles.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:20.690
When Hank got lost in his own mind, she basically
guided him back to sanity.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:21.810
Quantum healing

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.210
Most of the story arc involving Ghost, a.k.a.
Ava Starr, deals with her search for a way

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.820
to cure her quantum phase-shifting condition.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.470
Her powers made for some visually amazing
fight scenes, but her character is also in

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:35.930
constant pain and inching closer to the grave
with every moment.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.560
So that part's not good.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.750
To end her suffering, Ava concocts a plan
to ambush Janet Van Dyne on her way out of

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.850
the Quantum Realm and siphon Janet's stored
quantum energy.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:49.590
To do so, she uses a sleep chamber built to
help stave off the effects of her condition,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.230
although nobody ever explains exactly what
it is.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:56.370
By all appearances, it's designed to focus
or manipulate quantum particles.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.200
In a pinch, though, it can apparently draw
particles into itself.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.870
It turns out that there was no need to fight
about it though, because Janet is more than

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.270
happy to cure Ava.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.040
Infinity fallout

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.230
In case you still haven't seen Avengers: Infinity
War, fair warning: We're about to get into

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.719
some tiny spoilers here.

00:02:12.719 --> 00:02:17.010
By the end of Ant-Man and the Wasp, everything's
been patched up in the Ant-Man universe.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.939
And then like a punch to the face, the mid-credits
scene came along to remind us that this happy

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:26.010
little Ant-Man universe actually exists within
the big, mean MCU, where Thanos beat the Avengers

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.280
and dusted half the universe.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.139
As the first mid-credits scene shows for an
instant, Hank, Hope, and Janet are now on

00:02:31.139 --> 00:02:34.430
the list of finger-snap casualties.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.430
Shrinking timeline

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:39.409
With that major connection to Infinity War,
it's worth taking a moment to clarify the

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:42.349
timeline of everything that happened in Ant-Man
and the Wasp.

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:46.299
Despite being released after Infinity War,
Ant-Man and the Wasp takes place before the

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.480
events of that film.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.359
Right before it, by all accounts.

00:02:49.359 --> 00:02:53.120
The movie doesn't mention how much time has
passed between the main film and the mid-credits

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.739
scenes, but however long it was, that time
gap essentially contained Infinity War.

00:02:57.739 --> 00:03:01.829
When Scott jumps into the quantum tunnel,
Thanos is presumably finishing up his gauntlet

00:03:01.829 --> 00:03:07.099
over in Wakanda, putting the ending of both
movies at just about the same moment, chronologically.

00:03:07.099 --> 00:03:10.859
But this connection also leads to some interesting
new developments for Infinity War.

00:03:10.859 --> 00:03:14.079
Marvel mastermind Kevin Feige has been pretty
up front about that.

00:03:14.079 --> 00:03:18.540
"Ant-Man and the Wasp also connects directly
to Avengers 4.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.190
These characters are gonna be very important
going forward."

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.730
If that's the case, then there's a good chance
that all the fallen heroes in Infinity War

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:26.980
will make a comeback.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:31.129
It could be that Hope, Hank, and Janet - along
with the rest of the casualties of Thanos'

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:35.389
finger snap - weren't destroyed outright,
but instead transferred into the Quantum Realm.

00:03:35.389 --> 00:03:37.620
And speaking of that place...

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.329
Lost in the quantum realm

00:03:39.329 --> 00:03:42.719
Ant-Man and the Wasp certainly left one of
its heroes in a big cliffhanger.

00:03:42.719 --> 00:03:46.449
When the Van Dynes disintegrated while Scott
was in the Quantum Realm, he apparently got

00:03:46.449 --> 00:03:47.449
stuck there.

00:03:47.449 --> 00:03:50.909
Not only are the people who know how to get
him out gone, but they're probably also the

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:52.709
only people who even know he's in there.

00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:57.121
That opens up an interesting possibility:
After spending a long time in the Quantum

00:03:57.121 --> 00:04:00.739
Realm, Janet Van Dyne learned how to manipulate
quantum particles.

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:05.060
If Scott spends enough time sandwiched between
realities, he could feasibly develop the same

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.060
ability.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.879
That would give him a definite upper hand
against Thanos in the future, especially if,

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:14.379
as fans have speculated, the Infinity Stones
are somehow tied into the Quantum Realm.

00:04:14.379 --> 00:04:15.819
Thanks for watching!

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:18.509
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:18.509 --> 00:04:20.769
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

